WEBVTT

1
00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:22.680
INVENTING ESTONIA

2
00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:36.520
But I am already 6!
- I am already 7!

3
00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:39.600
But when was your birthday?

4
00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:44.160
I'll be on next Monday...

5
00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:47.960
Not this Monday, but the next...
I'll be 7.

6
00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:53.280
My mom keeps saying,
"This Monday, this Monday..."

7
00:00:54.440 --> 00:01:00.360
But now I am sure that
it's the next. Not this Monday.

8
00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:05.280
Mati! Where are your gloves?

9
00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:07.280
Sassu's gloves are here.

10
00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:11.880
I am at my grandfather's place.
I like to play with other children.

11
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:15.480
I visit my grandpa
almost every day in the evenings.

12
00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:21.000
Do you like
fine or coarse ground oatmeal? - Well...

13
00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:25.240
Like you have now? Instant oatmeal?
- Yes.

14
00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:27.400
This tastes better?
- Yes.

15
00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:31.840
One morning it happened that I had
no strength to blow on the porridge

16
00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:36.360
and it was so hot.
Oh...! So warm, like...

17
00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:40.720
I can't even say it.
And my soul was tired also.

18
00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:46.000
But the porridge was really important.
We had to get it in the tummy somehow.

19
00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:48.640
It was not so easy all the time.

20
00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:52.920
And then we put this thing
on this base.

21
00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:56.280
Sass made a picture.
I mean, he drew a picture. - Yes.

22
00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:58.880
How this thing might look like...

23
00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:03.000
And grandpa got the easy task.
He took a saw and a hammer and...

24
00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:06.160
Done!
Turn it on.

25
00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:09.760
Look, it is important
to hold it straight.

26
00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:15.400
Is it straight?
- Like that. Push the button.

27
00:02:17.720 --> 00:02:20.760
This is a porridge cooler.
Here we have a button.

28
00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:24.000
When you push it,
this propeller starts turning.

29
00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:27.480
I'll show you.
You turn it on like that...

30
00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:31.680
And then the cool air
gets in from here.

31
00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:34.400
And pushes it down here.

32
00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:36.880
So, we turn it on.

33
00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:45.560
See?

34
00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:53.720
Perfectly cooled porridge.

35
00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:56.200
It is so cool to be with grandpa.

36
00:02:56.320 --> 00:03:01.600
He is a great inventor. He is always
making cool things for children.

37
00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:03.920
All kinds of woodcarving stuff.

38
00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:09.080
But there is one thing...
You cannot argue with him.

39
00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:10.760
And I don't like it.

40
00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:19.760
But me... I'm such a boy...
Just a great guy.

41
00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:26.080
I like sport. It's my favorite.
I like bicycling.

42
00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:33.960
I'd like to ride to Nõmme and back
every day. To eat donuts!

43
00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:38.560
How many donuts will we have?
- Let's take two.

44
00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:43.640
A cocoa for me as well.
Let me have a great day.

45
00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:50.400
So, if we go to a donut shop,
then it has been a great day, right?

46
00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:55.240
That's good.

47
00:03:56.680 --> 00:04:01.840
Let's make a deal that today you'll
eat grandpa's donut as well. - Yeah!

48
00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:10.680
Do you see the trees
with different colors? - Yes.

49
00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:13.920
The spruce is really dark green.
- Yes.

50
00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:16.000
But the others are yellow.

51
00:04:16.120 --> 00:04:20.760
Just a little breeze
and the leaves fall off! - Yeah!

52
00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:23.160
We must protect nature.

53
00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:27.920
In the old days
nature kept people alive.

54
00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:32.520
That's why I would like
to be the President.

55
00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:36.840
Then I would really say that...

56
00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:39.800
No, actually I would like
to be the Prime Minister.

57
00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:42.800
Because the Prime Minister
is a little more important.

58
00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:45.440
He can make more decisions.

59
00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:48.400
I think I would make the decision

60
00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:52.560
that they could cut
less trees in Estonia.

61
00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:56.640
But a Prime Minister can invent also!

62
00:04:56.760 --> 00:04:59.760
I'll be the Prime Minister
and an inventor.

63
00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:05.720
You have gained, like, 5 kilos!
- Yes! 5 kilos!

64
00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:10.200
Did you eat too many buns?
- No! Too many donuts!
